+The macOS archive migration is delivered as one coherent consumer and native-validation cohort. Published diagnostics, release signing, appcast generation, Homebrew rendering and release preflight consume the existing declared archive policy. Fresh releases require the declared signed payloads; historical ZIP remains eligible only when the preferred archive is absent. Raw GitHub REST inventory retains actual asset digests, and each archive signature, fragment, length and checksum remains bound to the selected bytes. Ordinary helper ZIP output, unrelated OS assets, immutable appcast attachments and newer-tag safeguards keep their existing owners. Manual OS selection, shared verification and release authorization remain unchanged.
